Each test method calls `_run_case` with fixed `num_bits` and `narrow_range`, so within a run the quantity `quant_max - quant_min` in `adjust_and_nudge` is constant. The function computes `diff_range = max_range - min_range` and then `scale = diff_range / (quant_max - quant_min)`. Because the denominator is a fixed positive integer for every tested configuration, any increase in `diff_range` between successive calls forces `scale` to increase as well. The test data in all 12 methods uses progressively larger `max_range - min_range`, so the invariant holds across the full set of runs.

## Answer
{"invariant_exists":true}
